--- !u!114 &826955853
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 826955850}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 72dcd122254073845a271b4898476ffc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  pages:
  - title: I. THE METABOLIC LEAP
    eraCode: LOWER PALEOLITHIC // 1.500.000 B.C.
    bodyText: 'By striking flint against pyrite, early Terrans sparked controlled

      exothermic
      reactions. Fire externalized digestion, shrinking the gut

      and diverting
      immense metabolic caloric energy directly into the neocortex.'
  - title: II. THE METALLURGIC FORGE
    eraCode: BRONZE & IRON AGE // 3.300 B.C.
    bodyText: 'Humans tamed the crucible. Smelting copper, tin, and iron ore

      from
      Earth''s mantle, they transformed brittle stones into tools

      of agriculture,
      monumental architecture, and celestial measurement.'
  - title: III. THE THINKING STONE
    eraCode: INFORMATION AGE // 2026 A.D.
    bodyText: 'In a poetic planetary loop, humanity returned to common sand.

      Purifying
      quartz into monocrystalline silicon and carving nanometer gates,

      Terrans
      taught the melted rock of their cradle planet how to think.'
  currentPageIndex: 0
  titleTextMesh: {fileID: 916489296}
  bodyTextMesh: {fileID: 240656382}
